    "q-141027": {
      "dom_id": "step-q141027",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "If $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-1)=0$, then $x=$",
      "worked_solution": "The logarithms share the same base, and so we can combine them using the product rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-1) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(8(x-1)) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the equation for $x$ using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8(x-1))} & ={e}^{0} \\\\ 8(x-1) & =1 \\\\ 8x-8 & =1 \\\\ 8x & =9 \\\\ x & =\\frac{9}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
