    "q-1128": {
      "dom_id": "step-q1128",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Solve the equation ${log}_{5}⁡(6)+{log}_{5}⁡(2{x}^{2})={log}_{5}⁡(48).$",
      "worked_solution": "The logarithms share the same base, so we can combine them using the product rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{5}⁡(6)+{log}_{5}⁡(2{x}^{2}) & ={log}_{5}⁡(48) \\\\ {log}_{5}⁡(6\\cdot 2{x}^{2}) & ={log}_{5}⁡(48) \\\\ {log}_{5}⁡(12{x}^{2}) & ={log}_{5}⁡(48)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the equation for $x$ using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{{log}_{5}⁡(12{x}^{2})} & ={5}^{{log}_{5}⁡(48)} \\\\ 12{x}^{2} & =48 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x=2$ or $x=-2$\n\nLet's now check for extraneous solutions by substituting them back into the original equation: \n\n- Substituting $x=2$ back into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{5}⁡(6)+{log}_{5}⁡(2\\cdot {2}^{2}) & \\overset{?}{=}{log}_{5}⁡(48) \\\\ {log}_{5}⁡(6)+{log}_{5}⁡(8) & \\overset{?}{=}{log}_{5}⁡(48) \\\\ {log}_{5}⁡(6\\cdot 8) & \\overset{?}{=}{log}_{5}⁡(48) \\\\ {log}_{5}⁡(48) & ={log}_{5}⁡(48).\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=2$ is a valid solution.\n\n- Substituting $x=-2$ back into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{5}⁡(6)+{log}_{5}⁡(2(-2)^{2}) & \\overset{?}{=}{log}_{5}⁡(48) \\\\ {log}_{5}⁡(6)+{log}_{5}⁡(8) & \\overset{?}{=}{log}_{5}⁡(48) \\\\ {log}_{5}⁡(6\\cdot 8) & \\overset{?}{=}{log}_{5}⁡(48) \\\\ {log}_{5}⁡(48) & ={log}_{5}⁡(48).\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=-2$ is a valid solution.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$x=\\pm 2.$\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
